KZ3 patch 1118 (SPU pass 103): upstream ps3recomp PR #445, the LS read/write diagnostics gate (MIT; author: tekulvw, https://github.com/sp00nznet/ps3recomp/pull/445). spu_ls_read128/write128 test one gate per direction
(g_spu_ls_rdiag / g_spu_ls_wdiag: -1 until the first access settles them, then nonzero only while SPU_LS_LOWREAD,
SPU_LS_WATCH, SPU_SMC_WATCH or SPU_WWS_PROBE is armed); the WWS buffer/code probes are opt-in (SPU_WWS_PROBE=1, they
were always on); the diagnostics run out of line (spu_ls_read_diag / spu_ls_write_diag); NEON quadword swap.
Merged with ours at the root: patch 1035's WWS range pre-test is replaced by the read gate; patch 1100's per-function
snapshot spu_ls_dbg_armed() becomes the two gates (2 loads per lifted function entry instead of 5, and the fast path
from the first settled access instead of after the WWS print caps); the new gates are SPU_READ_MOSTLY (1102); 1107's
out-of-line gated copies are unchanged. Not taken: the PR's spu_helpers.h NEON float rewrite and its
test_spu_float_exact.c (+CMake entry): our spu_helpers.h is KZ3's own (patch 1000 keeps it, no NEON section exists to
patch, and the test calls spu_*_ref helpers ours does not have); NEON is ARM only. SPU_LS_DIAG_GATES marks the patch
for the host tests (test_spu_ls_gate.c, test_spu_hot_helpers.c updated). Notes the RE notes Pass 103.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): upstream gates (#445 merged upstream) + 1100's cap macros.

